# opt-nout-last: nout=2 and then njmp=4 on a later @ line, which one wins (XPPAUT 8.2.2)?
# xpp: rows=3
# pc: ok
# ruling: matches: nout and njmp set one value, so the last entry wins, also across @ lines (crates/pc-ode/docs/language.md, Lists). PhaseCont lists both as njmp in the model info, with the last value.
x'=1
x(0)=0
aux v=x
@ total=4,dt=0.5,meth=euler,nout=2
@ njmp=4
